hadiths[143]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1880","[AI-translation] Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""Consult the orphan girl regarding herself, and her permission is her silence."
"1881","[AI-translation] From Bahz ibn Hakim: My father narrated to me from my grandfather (Mu'awiyah ibn Haydah) who said: I said, ""O Messenger of Allah, regarding our women, what may we approach of them and what must we leave?"" He said: ""Approach your tilth however you wish, and feed her when you eat, and clothe her when you clothe yourself, and do not strike the face, and do not beat."
"1882","[AI-translation] From Khuzaymah ibn Thabit from the Prophet (peace be upon him) who said: Approaching women in their anuses is unlawful."
"1883","[AI-translation] Anmari who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) was sitting with his companions, then he entered and came out having bathed. We said, ""O Messenger of Allah, did something happen?"" He said: ""Yes, so-and-so passed by me, and the desire for women fell into my heart, so I went to one of my wives and had intercourse with her. Do likewise, for among the best of your deeds is approaching the halal."
"1884","[AI-translation] From Anas, marfu'an: The most beloved names to Allah, the Exalted, are 'Abd Allah, 'Abd al-Rahman, and al-Harith."
"1885","[AI-translation] From Jabir: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: Detain your children until the intensity of the evening passes, for it is an hour in which the devils spread out."
"1886","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), marfu'an: If there comes to you one whose character and religion you are pleased with, then marry him off. If you do not do so, there will be tribulation in the land and widespread corruption."
"1887","[AI-translation] From Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: I returned from a journey and came to the Prophet (peace be upon him), and he said: ""When you come to your family, do a wise deed."" So when I came to my family, I said: ""The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: 'When you come to your family, do a wise deed.'"" She said: ""It is yours."
"1888","[AI-translation] From Talq who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: When one of you desires of his wife a need, let him come to her even if she is at the oven."
"1889","[AI-translation] From Abu Musa, that he heard the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) say: ""When a man wants to marry off his daughter, he should ask her permission."
"1890","[AI-translation] Huwayrith (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: When Allah—Majestic is His mention—intends to create a soul, and the man has intercourse with the woman, his fluid flies into every vein and sinew of hers. When it is the seventh day, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, brings forth for it every vein between it and Adam. Then he recited: ""In whatever form He willed, He assembled you."" (Al-Infitar 82:8)"
"1891","[AI-translation] From Sahl b. Abi Hathmah, traced back to the Prophet: If the intention to propose to a woman occurs to a man, there is no harm in him looking at her."
"1892","[AI-translation] From Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, traced back to the Prophet: When a woman spends from the food of her household without being wasteful, she has her reward for what she spent, and her husband has his reward for what he earned, and the treasurer has the like of that, none of them diminishing the reward of another in anything."
"1893","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, traced back to the Prophet: When a woman spends from her husband's earnings without his command, he has half of its reward."
"1894","[AI-translation] From Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: If a virgin marries a previously married woman, he stays with her for seven days, and if a previously married man marries a virgin, he stays with her for three days."
"1895","[AI-translation] From Anas b. Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""When a servant marries, he has completed half of his religion, so let him fear Allah regarding what remains."
"1896","[AI-translation] From Abu Humayd, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: If one of you proposes to a woman, there is no blame upon him in looking at her if he is only looking at her for the purpose of proposal, even if she does not know."
"1897","[AI-translation] From Jabir b. Abd Allah, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: If one of you proposes to a woman, if he is able to look at what calls him to marry her, let him do so."
"1898","[AI-translation] From Zayd b. Arqam, that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: When a man calls his wife, she must answer, even if she is on the back of a saddle."
"1899","[AI-translation] Irbad b. Sariyah, he said: I heard the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, say: ""When a man gives his wife to drink, he is rewarded."" So I went to her and gave her to drink, and I informed her of what I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family."
"1900","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas, traced back to the Prophet: When the sun sets, keep your children in, for it is an hour in which the devils spread out."
"1901","[AI-translation] Jabir said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""If any one of you arrives at night, let him not come to his family unexpectedly until the woman whose husband has been away shaves her pubic hair, and the unkempt woman combs her hair."
"1902","[AI-translation] From 'Abd Allah bin 'Amr, elevated: ""When a man owns a woman, her gift is not valid except with his permission."
"1903","[AI-translation] Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Four are from happiness: a righteous wife, a spacious dwelling, a righteous neighbor, and a comfortable mount. And four are from misery: an evil neighbor, an evil wife, an evil mount, and a narrow dwelling."
"1904","[AI-translation] From 'Aishah, elevated: ""Consult women regarding their private parts."" It was said: ""But a virgin is too shy to speak?"" He said: ""Her silence is her consent."
"1905","On the authority of ʿAlī, who said: When we departed from Mecca, the daughter of Ḥamza followed us, calling out: ""O uncle! O uncle!"" So I took her by the hand and handed her over to Fāṭima, saying: ""Here is your cousin's daughter."" When we arrived in Medina, I, Zayd, and Jaʿfar disputed over her. I said: ""I took her, and she is my cousin's daughter."" Zayd said: ""She is my brother's daughter."" Jaʿfar said: ""She is my cousin's daughter, and her maternal aunt is with me."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Jaʿfar: ""You resemble me in creation and character."" He said to Zayd: ""You are our brother and our freedman."" He said to me: ""You are from me and I am from you."" ""Hand her over to her maternal aunt, for the maternal aunt is like a mother."" I said: ""Will you not marry her to me, O Messenger of Allah ﷺ?"" He said: ""She is my brother's daughter through breastfeeding."""
"1906","[AI-translation] Aswad reported from his father, from his grandfather, that he married off a daughter of his, and they had with them kibr and gharabil. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, went out and heard the sound, so he said: ""What is this?"" It was said: ""Habbar has married off his daughter."" The Prophet, peace be upon him, said: ""Announce the marriage, announce the marriage! This is a marriage, not fornication."" He said: I said: ""And what is the kibr?"" He said: ""The large drum, and the gharabil are the cymbals."
"1907","[AI-translation] Kindi reported from his father, elevated: ""Consult the women concerning themselves."" They said: ""O Messenger of Allah, a virgin is shy."" He said: ""A previously married woman expresses herself with her tongue, and a virgin's consent is her silence."
"1908","[AI-translation] Abu Sa'id said: We captured captives on the day of Hunayn, and we sought their ransom. We asked the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, about 'azl. He said: ""Do what appears fitting to you, for whatever Allah has decreed will come to pass. Not from every water is a child created."
"1909","[AI-translation] Nu'man bin Bashir, elevated: ""Be just among your children, be just among your children, be just among your children."
"1910","[AI-translation] Mu'awiyah bin Qura reported from his uncle (the brother of Qura bin Iyas) that he used to come to the Prophet with his son and seat him in front of him. The Prophet, peace be upon him, said to him: ""Do you love him?"" He said: ""Yes, very much."" He said: Then the boy died. The Prophet, peace be upon him, said to him: ""Are you grieved over him?"" He said: ""Yes, O Messenger of Allah."" He said: ""Would it not please you, when Allah admits you to Paradise, to find him at one of its gates, opening it for you?"" He said: ""Yes."" He said: ""Then it will be so, if Allah wills."
"1911","[AI-translation] The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Shall I not inform you of your men in Paradise? The Prophet is in Paradise, the Siddiq is in Paradise, the martyr is in Paradise, the newborn is in Paradise, and the man who visits his brother in a part of the city—he visits him only for the sake of Allah—is in Paradise. Shall I not inform you of your women in Paradise?! Every loving and devoted woman, when she is angered or wronged, or her husband is angry, says: 'Here is my hand in your hand; I will not sleep until you are pleased.'"" It is reported from the hadith of Anas, Ibn 'Abbas, and Ka'b bin 'Ujrah, may Allah be pleased with them."
"1912","On the authority of Al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: Abu Bakr came asking permission to enter upon the Prophet (peace be upon him). He heard Aisha raising her voice at the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). He was given permission and entered, and said: ""O daughter of Umm Ruman!"" And he seized her, saying: ""Do you raise your voice at the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)?"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) interposed between him and her. When Abu Bakr left, the Prophet (peace be upon him) began saying to her, appeasing her: ""Do you not see that I have interposed between the man and you?"" Then Abu Bakr came again and asked permission to enter, and found him laughing with her. He was given permission and entered, and Abu Bakr said to him: ""O Messenger of Allah, include me in your peace as you included me in your war."""
"1913","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas: A man was sitting with the Prophet (peace be upon him) when his son came to him. He took him, kissed him, and seated him in his lap. Then his daughter came to him, so he took her and seated her by his side. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Would you not treat them equally?"" (Meaning his son and daughter in kissing them)."
"1914","[AI-translation] Zubayr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Would one of you perhaps beat his wife like the beating of a slave? The best of you are the best to their families."
"1915","On the authority of ʿĀmir, who said: I heard al-Nuʿmān ibn Bashīr delivering a sermon on the pulpit, and he said: “My father gave me a gift. ʿAmra bint Rawāḥa said: ‘I will not be pleased until you have the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) witness it.’ So Bashīr came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and said: ‘I have given my son a gift.’ ʿAmra bint Rawāḥa said: ‘I will not be pleased until the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) witnesses it.’ He said: ‘Do you have other children besides him?’ He said: ‘Yes.’ He said: ‘Have you given all of them the like of what you gave him?’ He said: ‘No.’ He said: ‘This is injustice; so do not ask me to witness it. Fear Allah and treat your children justly, just as you would like them to be dutiful to you.’”"
"1916","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurayrah: It was said to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him): Which women are best? He said: ""The one who pleases him when he looks at her, obeys him when he commands her, and does not oppose him regarding herself or her wealth with what he dislikes."
"1917","[AI-translation] Narrated Aishah: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) mentioned Fatimah. She said: So I spoke, and he said: ""Are you not pleased to be my wife in this world and the Hereafter?"" I said: ""Yes."" He said: ""Then you are my wife in this world and the Hereafter."
"1918","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn Umar: A man came to the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) complaining against his father. He said: ""He has taken my wealth."" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said to him: ""Do you not know that you and your wealth are from the earnings of your father?"
"1919","[AI-translation] Narrated Jabir ibn Abdullah from the Prophet (peace be upon him): Verily, Iblis places his throne upon the water—and in one narration: the sea—then he dispatches his troops. The closest of them to him in station is the greatest of them in trial. One of them comes and says: ""I did such and such."" He says: ""You have done nothing."" He said: Then one of them comes and says: ""I did not leave him until I separated him from his wife."" He said: So he draws him near him and says: ""Excellent you are!"" Al-A'mash said: I think he said: ""He embraces him."
"1920","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn Umar, elevated [to the Prophet]: ""The greatest of sins before Allah is a man who marries a woman, and when he fulfills his need from her, he divorces her and takes away her dowry. And a man who employs a man, and takes away his wage. And another who kills an animal in vain."
"1921","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Verily, Allah has protective jealousy, and the believer has protective jealousy. The protective jealousy of Allah is that the believer commits what He has forbidden for him."
"1922","[AI-translation] Miqdam ibn Ma'di Karib that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) stood among the people, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: ""Verily, Allah enjoins you to treat women well, for they are your mothers, daughters, and maternal aunts. Verily, a man from the People of the Book marries a woman, and a thread suspends her hands, so neither of them desires to part from the other until they die of old age."
"1923","On the authority of Abu Sa'id, or Jabir, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) delivered a sermon, and he prolonged it, and he mentioned in it the matters of this world and the Hereafter. Then he mentioned: ""The first thing that caused the destruction of the Children of Israel was that the wife of the poor man would burden him with [demands for] clothes or jewelry, or he said: of the jewelry what the wife of the rich man would burden [her husband with]."" Then he mentioned a woman from the Children of Israel who was short, and she made for herself two legs of wood, and a ring that had a clasp and a lid, and she stuffed it with musk. And she went out between two tall women, or two stout women. So they sent a man to follow them, and he recognized the two tall women, but he did not recognize the owner of the two wooden legs."
"1924","[AI-translation] Narrated Aishah: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Your children are a gift from Allah to you. He gives to whom He wills daughters, and He gives to whom He wills sons (Ash-Shura 49). So they and their wealth are yours when you need it."
"1925","[AI-translation] Narrated Umm Salamah: The Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, took an oath to abstain from his wives for a month. When twenty-nine days had passed, he went to them in the morning or evening. It was said to him: ""Did you swear not to enter for a month?"" He replied: ""The month is twenty-nine days."
"1926","[AI-translation] Narrated Jabir ibn Abdullah: He heard the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, say: ""If I live, by Allah's will, I will prohibit that anyone be named Barakah, Nafi', and Aflah."" I do not know if he said ""Aflah"" or not, but the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, passed away without having prohibited it."
"1927","[AI-translation] Nu'man ibn Bashir: His father gifted him a gift, and he wanted the Prophet, peace be upon him, to witness it. He asked: ""Did you gift all your children as you gifted him?"" He replied: ""No."" The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""You are obligated to be just among your children just as they are obligated to honor you."
"1928","On the authority of ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥusayn, that al-Miswār ibn Makhramah narrated: When they arrived in Medina from Yazīd ibn Muʿāwiyah after the killing of al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), al-Miswār ibn Makhramah met him and said: ""Do you have any need of me that you would command me to fulfill?"" He said: ""I said to him: No."" He said to him: ""Will you give me the sword of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)? For I fear that the people may overpower you and take it from you. And by Allah! If you give it to me, it shall never reach anyone until my soul departs. For ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib proposed to the daughter of Abū Jahl alongside Fāṭimah, and I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) addressing the people concerning this on this pulpit of his, while I was that day of age (muḥtalim). He said: 'Fāṭimah is a part of me, and I fear she may be tried in her religion.' Then he mentioned a son-in-law of his from Banū ʿAbd Shams, and praised him for his marriage alliance with him, saying: 'He spoke to me and was truthful, and promised me and fulfilled his promise to me. And I do not make lawful what is unlawful, nor do I make unlawful what is lawful. But by Allah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and the daughter of the enemy of Allah shall never be together in one place ever.' And in another narration: 'with one man ever.'"""
"1929","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""A woman is created from a rib. She will never be straight for you on any path. If you enjoy her, you enjoy her while she has a crookedness. If you attempt to straighten her, you will break her, and breaking her is divorcing her."
"1930","[AI-translation] Ansariyyah: The Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, proposed to Umm Mubashshir bint al-Bara' ibn Ma'rur. She said: ""I made it a condition with my husband that I would not marry after him."" The Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""That is not valid."
"1931","[AI-translation] Narrated Masruq and Amr ibn Utbah: They wrote to Subai'ah bint al-Harith asking her about her affair. She wrote back to them: She gave birth twenty-five nights after the death of her husband. She adorned herself to seek a proposal, but Abu al-Sanabil ibn Ba'kak passed by her and said: ""You have acted hastily. Observe the longer of the two waiting periods—four months and ten days."" She said: I went to the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, seek forgiveness for me."" He asked, ""And why is that?"" I informed him, and he said: ""If you find a suitable husband, then marry."
"1932","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah: A man intended to marry a woman from the women of the Ansar. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Did you look at her? For there is something in the eyes of the Ansar."" Meaning smallness."
"1933","[AI-translation] Mughirah ibn Shu'bah: He proposed to a woman, and the Prophet, peace be upon him, said: ""Look at her, for it is more likely to bring about harmony between you."
"1934","[AI-translation] Narrated Husayn ibn Mihhsan, from his paternal aunt (it is said her name was Asma'): She entered upon the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, for some need, and he fulfilled her need. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said to her: ""Do you have a husband?"" She said: ""Yes."" He said: ""How are you with him?"" She said: ""I do not fall short in anything except what I am incapable of doing."" He said: ""Consider your position with him, for he is your Paradise and your Hell."
"1935","[AI-translation] The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Women are the counterparts of men."" (It comes from the hadith of Aisha and Anas, in which there is a story.)"
"1936","[AI-translation] From Fatimah bint Qays, she said: I came to the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) and said, ""I am the daughter of the family of Khalid, and my husband so-and-so has sent me my divorce, and I asked his family for maintenance and lodging, but they refused me."" They said, ""O Messenger of Allah, he has sent her three pronouncements of divorce."" She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said, ""Maintenance and lodging are only for a woman if her husband has the right of return over her."
"1937","[AI-translation] Mughirah bin Shu'bah, he said: When I arrived in Najran, they asked me, saying: ""You recite: 'O sister of Harun' (Maryam: 28), while Musa was before 'Isa by such and such."" So when I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family), I asked him about that, and he said: ""They used to name (their children) after their prophets and the righteous before them."
"1938","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""I declare forbidden the violation of the rights of two weak ones: the orphan and the woman."
"1939","[AI-translation] From 'Aishah, the wife of the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family), she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) was commanded to give his wives a choice, he began with me and said: ""I am going to mention a matter to you, so there is no harm upon you if you do not hasten until you consult your parents."" She said: And he knew that my parents would not command me to part with him. She said: Then he said: ""Indeed, Allah said: 'O Prophet, say to your wives...' (Al-Ahzab 28-29) until the completion of the two verses."" So I said to him: ""In what matter should I consult my parents? For I desire Allah, His Messenger, and the Home of the Hereafter."
"1940","[AI-translation] Ansariyyah, she said: The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) passed by me while I was among my female companions. He greeted us with peace and said: ""Beware of the ingratitude of the endowed."" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! What is the ingratitude of the endowed?"" He said: ""Perhaps one of you remains unmarried in her parents' house for a long time and grows old, until Allah, Mighty and Majestic, provides her with a husband, and provides her from him wealth and children. Then she becomes angry and shows ingratitude, saying: 'I have never seen any good from you.'"
"1941","[AI-translation] From 'Abdullah bin 'Abbas, raised to the Prophet: ""The previously married woman has more right to herself than her guardian, and the virgin is to be consulted regarding herself, and her silence is her permission."
"1942","[AI-translation] From 'Aishah, she said: A man called Shihab was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""You are Hisham."
"1943","[AI-translation] From 'Aishah, raised to the Prophet: ""Choose well for your seed, so marry the compatible, and give in marriage to them."
"1944","[AI-translation] From Abu Umamah, raised to the Prophet: ""Marry, for I will boast of your numbers among the nations on the Day of Resurrection, and do not be like the monasticism of the Christians."
"1945","On the authority of ʿĀʾishah, she said: She was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey while she was a young girl. She said: ""I had not yet put on flesh nor grown plump."" He said to his companions: ""Go ahead."" So they went ahead. Then he said: ""Come, let me race you."" So I raced him and I outran him on foot. Then, after a while (and in another narration: ""He left me be until I had put on flesh, grown plump, and forgotten""), I went out with him on a journey. He said to his companions: ""Go ahead."" So they went ahead. Then he said: ""Come, let me race you."" And I forgot what had been, and I had put on flesh. So I said: ""How can I race you, O Messenger of Allah, while I am in this condition?"" He said: ""You shall surely do it."" So I raced him and he outran me. Then (he began to laugh and) he said: ""This is for that former outrunning."""
"1946","[AI-translation] Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""A woman is married for one of three traits: a woman is married for her wealth, a woman is married for her beauty, and a woman is married for her religion. So take the one with religion and good character, may your right hand be rubbed in dust."
"1947","[AI-translation] Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him, raised to the Prophet: Three men supplicate to Allah but their supplication is not answered: a man who has an ill-tempered wife and does not divorce her, a man who is owed money by another man but did not take witnesses against him, and a man who gives his wealth to a foolish person, when Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, has said: ""And do not give the foolish your wealth"" (An-Nisa: 5)."
"1948","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas, raised to the Prophet: The previously married woman has more right to herself than her guardian, and the virgin's father seeks her permission regarding herself, and her permission is her silence."
"1949","[AI-translation] From Aishah, she said: An old woman came to the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, while he was at my place. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said to her: ""Who are you?"" She said: ""I am Juthamah al-Muzaniyyah."" He said: ""Rather, you are Hassanah al-Muzaniyyah. How are you? How is your condition? How have you been since we parted?"" She said: ""Well, may my father and mother be ransomed for you, O Messenger of Allah."" When she left, I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, you show such attention to this old woman?"" He said: ""She used to visit us during the time of Khadijah, and indeed, keeping good bonds is part of faith."
"1950","[AI-translation] From Abu Kabshah, raised to the Prophet: The best of you are the best of you to their families."
"1951","[AI-translation] Wahhab ibn Bakht, raised to the Prophet: ""The best of names are Abdullah and Abd al-Rahman, the most truthful of names are Hamam and Harith, and the worst of names are Harb and Murrah."
"1952","[AI-translation] Sadafi that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""The best of your women are the affectionate, the childbearing, the agreeable, the sympathetic, when they fear Allah. And the worst of your women are those who make a public display and are arrogant; they are the hypocrites, and none of them will enter Paradise except like the red-footed crow."
"1953","[AI-translation] From Uqbah ibn Amir, raised to the Prophet: The best of marriages are the easiest ones."
"1954","[AI-translation] From Aishah, raised to the Prophet: ""The best of you are the best of you to their families, and when your companion dies, leave him."
"1955","[AI-translation] From Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""The best of you are the best of you to their families, and I am the best of you to my family. And when your companion dies, leave him."
"1956","[AI-translation] From Aishah, she said: I did not realize until Zainab entered upon me without permission while she was angry. Then she said: ""O Messenger of Allah, do you think if the little daughter of Abu Bakr rolls up her forearms?"" Then she turned to me and I turned away from her until the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""Go ahead, take your revenge."" So I turned to her until I saw that her saliva had dried in her mouth and she could not reply to me with anything. Then I saw the Prophet, peace be upon him, with his face beaming."
"1957","[AI-translation] Rahman bin Salim bin 'Utbah bin 'Uwaym bin Sa'idah, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: You should marry virgins, for they have the sweetest mouths, the most productive wombs, and are the most content with little."
"1958","[AI-translation] From 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: I said, ""O Messenger of Allah, what if you came down to a valley in which there was a tree that had been eaten from, and you found a tree that had not been eaten from, in which of them would you let your camel graze?"" He said, ""In the one that had not been grazed from."" She meant that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him and his family, did not marry a virgin other than her."
"1959","On the authority of Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him): A man from the Ansar had two stallions that became unruly/mature. He put them in a walled garden and locked the door on them. Then he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanting him to supplicate for him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting with a group of the Ansar. The man said: ""O Prophet of Allah, I have come for a need, and I have two stallions that became unruly, so I put them in a walled garden and locked the door on them, and I would like you to supplicate for me that Allah may subdue them for me."" He said to his companions: ""Stand up with us."" So he went until he reached the door and said: ""Open it."" The door was opened, and one of the two stallions was near the door. When it saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), it prostrated to him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Bring me something to tie its head with, and give me control over it."" He brought a rope/halter, so he tied its head and gained control over it. Then they walked to the far end of the garden to the other stallion. When it saw him, it fell down prostrating. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the man: ""Bring me something to tie its head with."" So he tied its head and gained control over it, and said: ""Go, for they will not disobey you."" When the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw that, they said: ""O Messenger of Allah, these are two stallions that do not reason, yet they prostrated to you. Should we not prostrate to you?"" He said: ""I do not command anyone to prostrate to anyone. And if I were to command anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would have commanded the woman to prostrate to her husband."""
"1960","[AI-translation] Sulami who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him and his family, whenever a man came to him with a name he did not like, he would change it."
"1961","[AI-translation] The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him and his family, whenever he intended to marry off one of his daughters, would sit by her curtain and say: ""So-and-so mentions so-and-so,"" naming her and naming the man who mentions her. If she remained silent, he would marry her off, and if she disliked it, she would tap the curtain. If she tapped it, he would not marry her off. Narrated from the hadith of 'A'ishah, Abu Hurayrah, Ibn 'Abbas, and Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with them."
"1962","[AI-translation] From 'A'ishah, she said: The Prophet, peace be upon him, whenever he heard an ugly name, he would change it. He passed by a village called 'Afra, and he named it Khadirah."
"1963","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah: The name of Zaynab was Barrah, so it was said, ""She praises herself."" So the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, named her Zaynab."
"1964","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him and his family, would stick out his tongue to al-Hasan bin 'Ali, and the child would see the redness of his tongue and be delighted by it."
"1965","[AI-translation] From 'Umar: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him and his family, had divorced Hafsah, then he took her back."
"1966","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him and his family, used to order his daughters and his women to go out for the two Eids."
"1967","[AI-translation] From 'A'ishah: That the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, used to change an ugly name to a good name."
"1968","[AI-translation] From Anas: The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) used to play with Zaynab bint Umm Salama while saying: ""O Zuwaynab! O Zuwaynab!"" repeatedly."
"1969","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas who said: Juwayriya's name was Barra, so the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) changed her name to Juwayriya, and he disliked it being said: ""He left from Barra's."
"1970","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Nothing has been seen for two who love one another like marriage."
"1971","[AI-translation] From Zayd bin Arqam, that Muadh said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Have you seen the People of the Book prostrating to their bishops and patriarchs? Should we not prostrate to you?"" He said: ""If I were to command anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would command the woman to prostrate to her husband. And a woman does not fulfill the right of her husband until if he were to ask her for herself on a wooden saddle, she would give it to him."
"1972","[AI-translation] From Abdullah bin Amr, marfu: ""There is no divorce for a man regarding what he does not own, no manumission regarding what he does not own, and no sale regarding what he does not own."
"1973","[AI-translation] From Aishah, marfu: ""There is no burden from his two parents upon the child of zina. And no bearer of burdens bears the burden of another."
"1974","[AI-translation] From Wathilah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""It is not for a woman to dispose of anything from her wealth except with the permission of her husband."
"1975","[AI-translation] As was the asabah of her sons, so he took them out to Sham where they died. Amr bin al-As then arrived, and a mawla of hers died leaving wealth. Her brothers disputed with him before Umar bin al-Khattab. Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Whatever the child or the parent acquires belongs to his asabah, whoever he may be."
"1976","[AI-translation] From Amr bin Umayya, marfu: ""Whatever a man gives his wife is a sadaqah."
"1977","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah: Some women came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! We cannot reach you in your assembly because of the men, so appoint a day for us to come to you."" He said: ""Your appointment is the house of so-and-so."" He came to them on that day and for that appointment. He said: Among what he said to them was: ""There is no woman whose three children die, seeking reward, except that she enters Paradise."" A woman from among them said: ""Or two?"" He said: ""Or two."
"1978","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: ""There is no newborn among the children of Adam except that Satan touches him when he is born, so he cries out screaming from the touch of Satan, except Maryam and her son."" Then Abu Hurairah said: ""And I seek refuge for her in You and for her offspring from Satan, the expelled"" (Aal Imran: 36)."
"1979","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn Abbas, elevated to the Prophet: ""There is no Muslim who has two daughters reach maturity and he treats them well during their companionship with him, except that they will admit him into Paradise."
"1980","[AI-translation] Narrated Habibah or Umm Habibah: We were in the house of Aishah when the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, entered and said: ""There are no two Muslims who have three children die before reaching the age of accountability, except that they are brought until they are stopped at the gate of Paradise. It will be said to them: 'Enter Paradise.' They will say: 'Shall we enter while our parents have not entered?' It will be said to them—I do not know if it was the second time—'Enter Paradise, you and your parents.'"" He said: That is the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: ""So their intercession will not benefit them"" (Al-Muddaththir: 48). He said: The intercession of their children benefited the fathers."
"1981","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn Mas'ud that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, addressed the women and said to them: ""There is no woman among you who has three children die, except that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will admit her to Paradise."" An elderly woman among them said: ""O Messenger of Allah! And the mother of two?"" He said: ""And the mother of two is in Paradise."
"1982","[AI-translation] Narrated Jabir bin Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with them both: When Hafs bin Al-Mughirah divorced his wife Fatimah, she came to the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family. He said to her husband: ""Provide for her."" He said: ""I do not find anything to provide her."" He said: ""There must be a provision."" He said: ""Provide for her, even if half a sa' of dates."
"1983","[AI-translation] Narrated Aishah, the wife of the Prophet, peace be upon him: A woman came to me along with her two daughters, and she asked me, but I did not find anything with me except a single date. So I gave it to her. She took it, divided it between her two daughters, and did not eat anything from it. Then she stood up and left with her two daughters. The Prophet, peace be upon him, entered upon me and I informed him of her story. The Prophet, peace be upon him, said: ""Whoever is tested with daughters in any way and treats them well, they will be a shield for him from the Fire."
"1984","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah, elevated to the Prophet: ""Whoever has intercourse with women in their anuses has disbelieved."
"1985","[AI-translation] Narrated a man from Muzaynah: His mother said to him: ""Will you not go and ask the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, just as people ask him?"" So I went to ask him and found him standing and delivering a sermon. He was saying: ""Whoever seeks to remain chaste, Allah will keep him chaste. Whoever seeks independence, Allah will enrich him. Whoever asks people while he has the equivalent of five awaq has asked with importunity."" So I said to myself: A she-camel of mine is better than five awaq, and my servant has another she-camel which is better than five awaq, so I returned and did not ask him."
"1986","[AI-translation] Anmari: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, was sitting with his companions. He entered, then came out having performed ghusl. We said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Did something happen?"" He said: ""Yes, so-and-so passed by me and the desire for women occurred in my heart, so I went to one of my wives and had relations with her. So do the same, for among the best of your deeds is coming to that which is lawful."
"1987","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Whoever incites a maid servant against her family is not from us, and whoever corrupts a woman against her husband is not from us."
"1988","[AI-translation] From 'Adiyy bin Hatim, raised to the Prophet: ""Whoever embraces an orphan of his own or of another until Allah enriches him, Paradise is due for him."
"1989","[AI-translation] Anas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever supports two daughters or three daughters, or two sisters or three sisters, until they die (and in a narration: until they grow up, and in another: until they reach adulthood) or he dies before them, I and he will be like these two."" And he gestured with his index and middle fingers."
"1990","[AI-translation] From Jabir, raised to the Prophet: ""Whoever supports three daughters, suffices them, shows mercy to them, and treats them with kindness, he is in Paradise."
"1991","[AI-translation] Anas bin Malik said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever supports two girls until they reach adulthood will come on the Day of Resurrection, I and he"" and he joined his fingers together."
"1992","[AI-translation] From Anas, raised to the Prophet: ""Whoever has two sisters or two daughters and does good to them as long as they are with him, I and he will be in Paradise like these two."" And he joined his two fingers together."
"1993","[AI-translation] Uqbah bin Amir said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) saying: ""Whoever has three daughters, and is patient with them, and feeds them, gives them drink, and clothes them from his wealth, they will be a barrier for him from the Fire on the Day of Resurrection."
"1994","[AI-translation] Jabir bin Abdullah narrated to them, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever has three daughters, shelters them, suffices them, and shows mercy to them, Paradise is absolutely due for him."" A man from among the people said: ""And two, O Messenger of Allah?"" He said: ""And two."
"1995","[AI-translation] Anas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever has three daughters or three sisters, and fears Allah and maintains them, will be with me in Paradise like this."" And he gestured with his index and middle fingers."
"1996","[AI-translation] Jabir bin Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""Whoever has three daughters, shelters them, shows mercy to them, and sponsors them, Paradise is absolutely due for him."" He said: It was said, ""O Messenger of Allah, what if there are two?"" He said: ""And if there are two."" He said: Some of the people thought that if they had said to him ""one,"" he would have said ""one."
"1997","On the authority of Abu Umamah from Amr ibn Abasah al-Sulami, who said: I said to him: ""Narrate to us a hadith that you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, in which there is no deficiency and no error."" He said: I heard him say:1. ""Whoever has three children born to him in Islam, and they die before reaching the age of puberty, Allah Almighty will admit him to Paradise by His mercy towards them.""2. ""And whoever gets a gray hair in the path of Allah Almighty, it will be a light for him on the Day of Resurrection.""3. ""And whoever shoots an arrow in the path of Allah Almighty, and it reaches the enemy, whether it hits or misses, it will be for him like the reward of freeing a slave.""4. ""And whoever frees a believing slave, Allah will free from the Fire a limb of his for every limb of the slave.""5. ""And whoever spends a pair in the path of Allah Almighty, then Paradise has eight gates, and Allah Almighty will admit him into Paradise from whichever gate He wills."""
"1998","[AI-translation] He (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""The two who invoke curses, if they separate, will never come together again."" (It was reported from the hadith of Ibn Umar, Sahl bin Sa'd, Abdullah bin Mas'ud, and Ali bin Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with them.)"
"1999","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah from the Prophet (peace be upon him) that he said: The women who seek Khula' and the women who extort are the hypocrites."
"2000","[AI-translation] Narrated 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr: A woman disputed with her husband over her child, so the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: The woman is more entitled to her child as long as she does not remarry."
"2001","[AI-translation] Narrated Salim bin 'Abdullah (ibn 'Umar) from his father from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him): He said: A woman is 'awrah, and when she goes out, Satan casts a glance at her, and she is closest to Allah when she is in the innermost part of her house."
"2002","[AI-translation] Narrated Maymun bin Mihran who said: Mu'awiyah proposed to Umm al-Darda' but she refused to marry him, and said: I heard Abu al-Darda' saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""A woman is with her last husband,"" or he said: ""for her last husband,"" or as she said, and I do not want anyone in place of Abu al-Darda'."
"2003","[AI-translation] Narrated 'Ali bin Abi Talib: He (peace be upon him and his family) forbade women from speaking (meaning in their homes) except with the permission of their husbands."
"2004","[AI-translation] Rabi' bin Sabrah Al-Juhani from his father: He (peace be upon him) forbade Mut'ah (at the time of the conquest, Mut'ah of women) and said: Verily, it is forbidden from this day of yours until the Day of Resurrection."
"2005","[AI-translation] Rabi' bin Sabrah Al-Juhani from his father: That the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) forbade Mut'ah and said: Verily, it is forbidden from this day of yours until the Day of Resurrection, and whoever has given anything, let him not take it back."
"2006","[AI-translation] Narrated Jabir bin 'Abdullah: He (peace be upon him and his family) forbade anal intercourse with women."
"2007","[AI-translation] Narrated 'A'ishah: She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: Marriage is part of my Sunnah, and whoever does not act upon my Sunnah is not of me. And marry, for I will boast of your numbers over the nations. And whoever has the means, let him marry; and whoever does not find it, then upon him is fasting, for indeed fasting is a shield (wija') for him."
"2008","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah: When the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) went out, he stopped at Thaniyyat al-Wada', and he saw lanterns and heard women crying. He said: ""What is this?"" They said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Women whose husbands had contracted Mut'ah with them."" So the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""Marriage, divorce, the waiting period, and inheritance have invalidated—or he said: forbidden—Mut'ah."
"2009","[AI-translation] He said, peace be upon him: ""This, then the backs of the mats."" He said this, peace be upon him and his family, to his wives during the Farewell Pilgrimage. It is reported from the hadith of Abu Waqad al-Laythi, Abu Hurayrah, Zaynab bint Jahsh, Sawdah bint Zam'ah, Umm Salamah, and 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them."
"2010","[AI-translation] Islamic period, he said: 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, proposed to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, for Fatimah, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with her, and he said: ""She is yours, on the condition that you maintain good companionship with her."
"2011","[AI-translation] From Sahl ibn Mu'adh ibn Anas from his father from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, that a woman came to him and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! My husband has departed as a warrior, and I used to follow his prayer when he prayed, and all his actions. So inform me of a deed that will bring me to the level of his deed until he returns."" He said to her: ""Are you able to stand and not sit, fast and not break the fast, and remember Allah, Blessed and Exalted, and not cease until he returns?"" She said: ""I cannot bear this, O Messenger of Allah!"" He said: ""By the One in Whose Hand my soul is, even if you were to undertake it, you would not attain a tenth of his deed until he returns."
"2012","[AI-translation] From Mu'adh ibn Jabal from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, he said: No woman harms her husband in this world except that his wife from among the maidens of Paradise says: ""Do not harm him, may Allah fight you! For he is but a guest with you, soon to depart from you to us."
"2013","[AI-translation] From Umm Salamah she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: A woman must not ask for the divorce of her sister (co-wife) so as to empty what is in her plate, for her provision is upon Allah."
"2014","Narrated Jabir ibn Abdullah: Abu Bakr entered seeking permission to enter upon the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) ... the hadith, and in it: The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) was sitting with his wives around him, asking him for maintenance. And the saying of Allah the Exalted was revealed: ""O Prophet, say to your wives..."" (Al-Ahzab: 28) until it reached: ""For the doers of good among you is a great reward"" (Al-Ahzab). He said: ""O Aisha! I want to propose a matter to you, and I would like you not to hasten in it until you consult your parents."" She said: ""What is it, O Messenger of Allah?"" So he recited the verse to her. She said: ""About you, O Messenger of Allah, should I consult my parents? Rather, I choose Allah, His Messenger, and the Home of the Hereafter. And I ask you not to inform any of your wives of what I have said."" He said: ""No woman among them will ask me except I will inform her. Indeed, Allah did not send me as a cause of hardship nor as one who makes things difficult, but He sent me as a teacher and a facilitator."""
"2015","[AI-translation] From 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, elevated to the Prophet: Do not dislike daughters, for they are the comforting and precious ones."
"2016","[AI-translation] From 'Ata ibn Yasar he said: A man came to the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Is there any sin upon me if I lie to my family?"" He said: ""No, but Allah does not love lying."" He said: ""O Messenger of Allah, I reconcile them and put their souls at ease."" He said: ""There is no sin upon you."
"2017","[AI-translation] From 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr, elevated to the Prophet: It is not permissible for a woman to give a gift (from her wealth) except with the permission of her husband."
"2018","[AI-translation] From 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Allah does not look at a woman who does not thank her husband, while she cannot do without him."
"2019","[AI-translation] From Jabir ibn 'Abdullah he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said to me: ""O Jabir! Do you have a wife?"" He said: I said: ""Yes."" He said: ""Did you marry a previously married woman or a virgin?"" He said: I said to him: ""I married her and she is a previously married woman."" He said: He said: ""Why did you not marry a young virgin?"" He said to him: ""My father was killed with you on such and such a day, and left behind young girls, so I disliked bringing to them a young girl like one of them, so I married a previously married woman who could pick the lice from one of them and sew the garment of one of them if it tore."" He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""How excellent is what you have seen."
"2020","[AI-translation] From 'Aisha, the wife of the Prophet (peace be upon him), she said: The Abyssinians entered the mosque playing, and he said to me: ""O Humayra', would you like to watch them?"" I said: ""Yes."" So he stood by the door, and I came to him and placed my chin on his shoulder, and rested my face against his cheek. She said: And among their saying that day was: ""Abu al-Qasim is good."" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Is it enough for you?"" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Do not hasten."" He stood, then said:"
"2021","On the authority of Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, who said: When the matter of Uthman ibn Maz'un arose — who had been abstaining from women — the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for him and said: ""O Uthman! I have not been commanded to practice monasticism. Have you turned away from my Sunnah?"" He said: ""No, O Messenger of Allah."" He said: ""Indeed, part of my Sunnah is that I pray and sleep, fast and break my fast, marry women and divorce them. So whoever turns away from my Sunnah is not of me. O Uthman! Verily, your family has a right over you, and your eye has a right over you."" Sa'd said: ""By Allah, there were men among the Muslims who had agreed that if the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had allowed Uthman to continue as he was, they would have castrated themselves and become celibate."""
"2022","[AI-translation] Muzanni that the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) said: An 'aqiqah is to be offered for the boy, and his head should not be wiped with blood."
